Checks for raspine-watchdog-health: one NAME.conf per service that must keep
running (shell, sourced). Packages drop their own here.

  NAME="Pi-Star MCP"                    what it is, for the log
  CHECK="raspine-watchdog-fresh /run/pistar/mcp-heartbeat 60"
                                        a command; exit 0 = healthy (killed
                                        after 20 seconds)
  RESTART="rc-service pistar-mcp restart"
                                        how to bring it back
  GRACE=300        seconds after boot, and after each restart, before it is
                   judged
  FAIL_AFTER=90    seconds unhealthy before anything is done
  RESTARTS=3       restarts before a recovery reboot

Unhealthy for FAIL_AFTER: restarted. Still unhealthy after RESTARTS
restarts: a recovery reboot, unless the loop guard says no (MAX_REBOOTS in
/etc/conf.d/raspine-watchdog). Events: /var/lib/raspine-watchdog/events.
